Linked List Insertion

Insertion means adding a new node to a linked list.

We will learn 3 important operations:

Insert at the Beginning
Insert at the End
Insert at a Specific Position

A singly linked list looks like:

10 → 20 → 30 → None
1. Insert at the Beginning

Suppose we want to insert 5.

Before:

10 → 20 → 30 → None

After:

5 → 10 → 20 → 30 → None

The important thing is to connect the new node to the old head, then make the new node the head.

